 - [Subsonic API Compatibility](https://www.navidrome.org/docs/developers/subsonic-api/)
 
+## Reverse proxy authentication
+
+Set `ReverseProxyWhitelist` to a comma-separated list of trusted proxy IPs or
+CIDR ranges, such as `127.0.0.1/8,2001:db8::/32`. The corresponding environment
+variable is `ND_REVERSEPROXYWHITELIST`. The default empty list disables proxy
+authentication. The special entry `@` trusts requests received over a Unix
+socket. Only the connection's source address is checked; forwarded IP headers
+cannot grant access.
+
+The proxy must send the authenticated username in `Remote-User`, or in the
+header named by `ReverseProxyUserHeader` (`ND_REVERSEPROXYUSERHEADER`). An
+optional `ReverseProxyDefaultUser` (`ND_REVERSEPROXYDEFAULTUSER`) is used when
+that header is absent. Users are created on their first proxy login, and the
+first user becomes an administrator. Restrict the whitelist to proxies that
+remove any client-supplied authentication header before setting their own.
+
